    {
      "id": "scene-01",
      "chapterId": "ch-harness",
      "title": "A model is not an agent",
      "template": "opening",
      "duration": 30,
      "knowledgeNodeIds": [],
      "captionMode": "bottom",
      "camera": {
        "zoomFrom": 1,
        "zoomTo": 1.03,
        "panX": 0.5,
        "panY": -0.2
      },
      "narration": [
        {
          "id": "scene-01-n1",
          "text": "A language model predicts the next token. Give it context and it writes a useful answer, but prediction alone cannot open a file or run a test.",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9.5
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-01-n2",
          "text": "To do real work, the model needs tools, memory, a workspace, and a way to see what happened after each action.",
          "start": 9.5,
          "end": 19
        },
        {
          "id": "scene-01-n3",
          "text": "That runtime is the harness. It is the difference between a model that talks and an agent that acts.",
          "start": 19,
          "end": 29
        }
      ],
      "elements": [
